hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"35","Subbūḥun, Quddūsun, Rabbul-malā'ikati warrūḥ. Glory (to You) , Most Holy (are You) , Lord of the angels and the Spirit. Reference: Muslim 1/353, Abu Dawud 1/230."
"36","Allāhumma laka raka`tu, wa bika 'āmantu, wa laka 'aslamtu khasha`a laka sam`ee wa baṣarī, wa mukhkhī, wa `aẓmī, wa `aṣabī, wa mastaqalla bihi qadamī. O Allah , to You I bow (in prayer) and in You I believe and to You I have submitted. Before You my hearing is humbled, and my sight, and my mind, my bones, my nerves and what my feet have mounted upon (for travel). Reference: Muslim 1/534, Abu Dawud, An-Nasa'i and At- Tirmidhi."
